{
  "info": {
    "name": "University Record Service",
    "description": "University Record through the Gateway where the Gateway serves it, otherwise on the instance itself. base_url is {{gateway}}/api/v1/university-record: since the Gateway's 4.0.0 (#110) it serves only the player route GET /records/{category} and the public GET /health of this service, and answers 404 on every other one. A player's request names the player in X-Player-Id, which the collection pre-request script turns into a signed Bearer JWT on a Gateway request. Run the 'scenario' folder top to bottom.\n\nLAB 4 (4.0.0). applicant.initialized, session.started and session.ended arrive from the Message Broker (topics events.<event_type>), not on POST /events, which is removed; this service's own applicant.initialized is published to events.applicant.initialized. Postman cannot send the broker's gRPC calls: the events of the scenario have to be published to the broker with the full envelope first (docs/UNIVERSITY_RECORD_SERVICE.md, \u00a711), and the session's scopes are set with the session-service mock (POST /admin/sessions/{id}/scopes).\n\nDIRECT CALLS. Every request whose route is not a Gateway route goes to one instance directly through {{university_record_direct_url}}, with the service's own path (/api/v1/..., /health/ready, /status, /logs, /metrics; no /university-record prefix): /health/ready, /status, /logs, /metrics, the scenario's step 4 (POST /admin/sessions/{id}/scopes) and step 9 (GET /applicants/{id}/records), POST /events, POST /applicants/next, every /admin/* request and the player-id-on-a-service-only-route edge case. The service validates no token but on GET /logs, which needs {{service_token}}: a direct service call carries no X-Service-Token and no X-Player-Id, and a direct request that plays a player sends X-Player-Id as it is (the pre-request script signs no JWT for a direct request). Direct and Gateway requests must reach the same database: in the team stack forward an instance's port (docs/UNIVERSITY_RECORD_SERVICE.md, \u00a711). The Gateway 3.1.0 still in the compose serves the Lab 3 routes too, until the compose runs its 4.0.0.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
